You have no search on this turn, so nothing here may be cited or looked up — but `emit_card` and `describe_card` are still yours, and `<cards>` still applies. Judge it by the ANSWER YOU ARE WRITING, not by this classification: if it sets out a Verfahren, a set of requirements, or a table of cases from what you already know, that is a card whether or not the turn was called conversational. An off-topic redirect and a piece of small talk are not, and get none. You have the card index but not this turn's card craft, so call `describe_card` for the shape before emitting — one call, and it is never a reason to skip a card the answer called for.
